PART I — GIT & GITHUB — 40 MARKS

1. Set up the codebase locally

git clone <repository-url>
cd "Apartment Management App"

2. Verify remote connections

git remote -v

3. Check staged, unstaged and untracked changes

git status

4. Create and directly switch to feature branch

git switch -c feature/tenant-registration

5. Show local, remote and current branch

git branch -a
git branch --show-current

6. Add specific file and commit

git add src/main/java/com/apartment/servlet/TenantServlet.java
git commit -m "Add tenant registration servlet"

7. Add missed file to last commit without changing message

git add src/main/webapp/WEB-INF/web.xml
git commit --amend --no-edit

8. Get remote updates WITHOUT changing local files

git fetch origin

Remember: fetch downloads remote changes but does not modify your working files.

9. Incorporate latest remote main into current branch

git pull origin main

10. Rebase feature branch onto updated main

git rebase origin/main

11. Cancel rebase and return to previous state

git rebase --abort

12. Undo faulty commit while preserving history

git revert <commit-hash>

13. Undo last commit but keep changes staged

git reset --soft HEAD~1

14. Remove file from Git but keep it locally

git rm --cached src/main/resources/db-config.env

15. Temporarily save unfinished changes

git stash

16. View stashes and restore latest stash

git stash list
git stash pop

17. Compare index.jsp between feature and main

git diff main..feature/tenant-registration -- src/main/webapp/index.jsp

18. Compact visual Git timeline

git log --oneline --graph --decorate --all

19. Merge feature into main

git switch main
git merge feature/tenant-registration

20. Push main and verify same commit point

git push origin main
git rev-parse HEAD
git rev-parse origin/main

If both hashes are identical → local and remote are at the same commit.

