Q3. Build Output Analysis

A. WAR filename

Maven normally generates:

artifactId-version.war

So if:

<artifactId>apartment-management</artifactId>
<version>0.0.1-SNAPSHOT</version>
<packaging>war</packaging>

then:

target/apartment-management-0.0.1-SNAPSHOT.war

Rule:

artifactId + "-" + version + ".war"

If <finalName> is specified, that name overrides the default.

Example:

<build>
    <finalName>apartment</finalName>
</build>

produces:

target/apartment.war

⸻

B. Context path

If the plugin contains:

<path>/apartment</path>

then the application is normally accessed at:

http://localhost:8080/apartment

