Q4. Maven Core Concepts

A. pluginManagement vs plugins

pluginManagement

<pluginManagement>
    <plugins>
        <plugin>
            ...
        </plugin>
    </plugins>
</pluginManagement>

Defines/configures plugins for inheritance or later use. It does not activate the plugin by itself.

plugins

<plugins>
    <plugin>
        ...
    </plugin>
</plugins>

Actually declares the plugin for the current project, so Maven can execute it.

Easy memory:

pluginManagement = configuration

plugins = activation/use

⸻

B. SNAPSHOT

0.0.1-SNAPSHOT

SNAPSHOT means the version is still under development and can change.

Unlike a release version, Maven may check repositories for a newer snapshot version during dependency resolution.

Release: stable/fixed version.

SNAPSHOT: development version that may be updated.

