B. Why provided for Servlet API?

<dependency>
    <groupId>javax.servlet</groupId>
    <artifactId>javax.servlet-api</artifactId>
    <version>4.0.1</version>
    <scope>provided</scope>
</dependency>

provided means the dependency is needed to compile the application but is already provided by the application server such as Tomcat at runtime.

If provided is omitted, the Servlet API can be packaged inside the WAR along with Tomcat’s own Servlet API, which can cause duplicate/incompatible classes and runtime conflicts.

